  "rationale": [
    "CAP-121 and CAP-126 already require deterministic FFmpeg/ffprobe media execution and post-production quality control, so this materializes an existing execution surface rather than adding a capability.",
    "FFmpeg 9.0.1 provides ONNX Runtime and OpenVINO DNN backends, but its ONNX CUDA path can fall back to CPU; FA3 therefore adds a fail-closed observed-provider check instead of inheriting silent fallback.",
    "Stable 9.0.1 dnn_processing does not accept CUDA hardware frames, while development trunk has CUDA-frame work; zero-copy DNN therefore remains capability-evidence gated rather than a stable baseline claim.",
    "Modern super-resolution, restoration and frame interpolation are better isolated behind a frame-server adapter such as VapourSynth/vs-mlrt and the existing inference-portability authority."
  ]
}
